---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import CanvasLab from "../../../components/CanvasLab.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<SiteLayout title="Canvas Lab — deterministic particles" description="An accessible, browser-native deterministic particle simulation with bounded controls, explicit play and pause, seed reset and a readable static fallback.">
  <div class="shell page-pad">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Lab home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Canvas Lab</nav>
    <header class="inner-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-led" aria-hidden="true"></span> LAB 002 / INTERACTIVE CANVAS</p>
      <h1>Canvas Lab<span class="heading-accent">.</span></h1>
      <p>Watch a small, repeatable physics world. Change particle density, control motion, and reset to exactly the same starting state.</p>
    </header>
    <CanvasLab />
    <section class="below-studio" aria-labelledby="canvas-details">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT THIS DEMONSTRATES</p><h2 id="canvas-details">Determinism over spectacle.</h2></div>
      <div><p>A seeded local random generator creates particles at fixed positions for a given canvas size. A pure TypeScript step function computes their movement and reflection. Browser rendering is separate from the simulation logic.</p><p>The animation starts paused, observes reduced-motion settings, stops when the page is hidden and caps render resolution on high-density screens. No WebGL, imported media, tracking or remote API is required.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ruslanudintsev-ai/ruslan-ai-lab/blob/feat/p2-canvas-core-20261031/src/domain/canvas.ts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the simulation source ↗</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
